# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Tracked vs. local. Source, configs, datasets small enough to review, and the
# evaluation baseline are tracked. Model weights, the knowledge base, its
# vectors, and archived run history are local-only: they move via the Hugging
# Face repos, never through git. See docs/WORKSPACE.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
pipeline/__pycache__/

# Secrets. The glob is deliberately wide: editors and shells write sidecars
# (.env.save, .env.local, .env.bak) that would otherwise land outside .env.
.env
.env*

# Tooling state
.claude/settings.local.json
.cache/

# Model artifacts — published on the Hub, never committed
*.gguf
*.safetensors
camus-*-merged/
camus_sft_merged/
camus_final_hf/
*.BACKUP.*
*.partial.*

# LoRA adapter weights (keep the folder's README + configs, ignore the binaries)
adapters/*
!adapters/README.md
!adapters/adapter_config.json
!adapters/tokenizer_config.json
!adapters/chat_template.jinja

# Knowledge base + embedding vectors: derived, large, and built from
# copyrighted sources. Both live untracked at the repo root.
*.npy
/camus_kb*.jsonl
/camus_kb_vectors*.npy
*.ollama.npy
data/camus_kb_full.jsonl
data/camus_kb_vectors.npy
data/source_chunks.jsonl
data/kb_extracted.jsonl
*.pdf

# A second vector file in the llama.cpp embedding family is kept beside the
# live one for reference by the hosted Space. The local stack must never load
# it; covered by *.npy above, named here so the intent is explicit.
camus_kb_vectors.llamacpp.npy

# NOTE: the five small training-corpus files (data/camus_*.jsonl) ARE tracked on
# purpose. camus_sft.jsonl (10 MB) is not — rebuild it with the Phase-1 batch
# pipeline in pipeline/ (see the README) if you need to retrain.
data/camus_sft.jsonl

# Staged upload bundles — assembled from tracked sources, never committed.
build/

# Local reference material and superseded run history — never published.
# Anchored to the root: an unanchored "archive/" also matches eval/archive/ and
# data/archive/ at any depth, which blocks the negation below.
/archive/
data/archive/

# Superseded eval runs stay local. Two exceptions are kept in the history
# because they are the record behind a decision: the base-model selection
# evidence, and the scored runs backing each released model version.
eval/archive/*
!eval/archive/base_selection/
!eval/archive/v2_*/
!eval/archive/v3_*/
!eval/archive/v4_*/
!eval/archive/v5_*/
!eval/archive/postrefactor_*/

# Inbound transfer bundles must never be committed.
*transfer_bundle*
*_transfer/
*.zip

# Local conversation memory — never commit; contains chat content.
# profile.md is per-user; a profile.example.md template is tracked instead.
/memory.jsonl
/memory_vectors.npy
/memory_pending.jsonl
/profile.md
# Human A/B evaluation sessions — real conversations, never published.
/eval_human/
# Probe fixtures: a real name, city, and project. memory_fixtures.example.json
# is committed as the template.
/memory_fixtures.json

# Primary sources (copyrighted books) and anything mined from them — local only.
/raw_books/
/sources/
data/drafts/
data/primary_*.jsonl

# Local-only working notes.
MISSING.md

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Kept locally, out of the public repo: training data, process history and one-off tools
data/camus_analysis.jsonl
data/camus_conversational.jsonl
data/camus_epistemic.jsonl
data/camus_multiturn.jsonl
data/camus_phase3.jsonl
data/camus_refusals.jsonl
data/camus_short.jsonl
data/cloud/
docs/archive/
